{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1510890-oh-glad-to-see-this-finally-come-out","id":1510890,"title":"Oh, glad to see this finally come out.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-06T09:57:23-07:00","id":1510890,"title":"Oh, glad to see this finally come out.","content":"I've been interested in this for a bit. Anyone with their hands on it know how Daredevils compare to Talents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T10:15:48-07:00","id":1510891,"title":"","content":"They <i>are </i>Talents. In the Flux-heavy world of Adventure, they get their Dramatic Editing on the cheap (Daredevils pay one less for DE than everyone else does, and they can pay with Momentum instead of Inspiration if they wish), and they have era-Specific Gifts available to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T14:09:06-07:00","id":1510912,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> <br /> Daredevil = Talent<br /> Mesmerist = Psiad<br /> Stalwart = Nova<br /> <br /> I understand that Mesmerists and Stalwarts are sort of the &quot;early release&quot; versions of their later counterparts, a taste of things to come. Does that mean that the abilities of those characters are limited most by the DeusExMachina Juice being at a lower level than in later eras, or is this more to do with the mindset of the people gifted with access to power? I'm waiting on my redemption code from the Trinity PG Kickstarter so I can do a full dive myself, but I'm curious because I'm doing some campaign world building and am considering some ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27972-gm-janus","name":"GM Janus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T15:23:52-07:00","id":1510922,"title":"","content":"They're limited by the Doyen imposition of an energy barrier around the Earth, which changed the dynamics of the Telluric Energies: they <i>would have been </i>full-powered Novas and psiads without that interference. And once Divas Mal shattered that barrier with <i>his </i>efforts almost a century later, they <i>were. </i><br /> <br /> But the same dynamic which suppressed the Quantum and Psi potentials <i>enhanced </i>the Flux users.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T15:55:54-07:00","id":1510924,"title":"","content":"Ah, OK, so the metaphysical interaction is that the Doyen Barrier sort gave Talents the time to... mature? Marinate? Still, good to know there is a series of events to lock things in for certain periods rather than a subjective &quot;That's just how folks were&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27972-gm-janus","name":"GM Janus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T16:08:28-07:00","id":1510925,"title":"","content":"The way one of the writers described it \u2014 unofficially, mind you \u2014 is that Quantum and Psi can be thought of as particles loosely bound together by Flux; and that combo is Telluric Energy. When the Doyen Barrier went up, it pressurized the mix, causing the Quantum and Psi particles into close proximity to each other, weakening their respective influences but leaving the bonds of Flux largely unaffected \u2014 except that, with it being pressurized, there are more Flux bonds present. Thus, the effects of Flux were intensified by the pressurization, while the effects of the Quantum and Psi were muted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T16:19:54-07:00","id":1510926,"title":"","content":"OK, I can get behind that logic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27972-gm-janus","name":"GM Janus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T20:59:54-07:00","id":1511043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1510890-oh-glad-to-see-this-finally-come-out?p=1510891#post1510891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>are </i>Talents. In the Flux-heavy world of Adventure, they get their Dramatic Editing on the cheap (Daredevils pay one less for DE than everyone else does, and they can pay with Momentum instead of Inspiration if they wish),</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say daredevils get Dramatic Editing cheap, but rather that everyone else pays a surcharge, since daredevils pay the exact same default costs as standard talents or Aether era squires.<br /> <br /> Having gone over the final download, I have to say I'm disappointed with one thing and very angry with another.<br /> <br /> My disappointment is with the fact that, since the preview copy was released over the x-mas/new year's holiday, I got less than 1/3 of the way through the book before the errata period closed. I didn't even get to the Gifts, and it looks like no one else submitted Gift errata either, since all of the things I noticed are still in the book. In addition to Momentary Gifts that should be Constant and vice versa, it looks like in the 'low powered' era of Adventure!, mesmerists are able to create illusions the size of cities and break machines the size of a city with a simple Gift and a single dice roll.<br /> <br /> I'm quite angry with the fact that, despite raising the issue during both the Kickstarter manuscript and preview book errata phases, they didn't change one single word of the Socialism entry of the seven evil '-isms' section of the storyguiding chapter. They give us page after page on the evils of anti-Semitism, classism, fascism, heterosexism, racism, and sexism\u200b, but follow it up with half a page of pro-socialist hype. The Holocaust killed about 6.5 million people, while Communist governments have killed anywhere from 10 million to 110 million, depending on the source.<br /> <br /> We get pretty phrases like &quot;They sought the replacement of capitalism with something more equal and rational with shared wealth within a given society&quot; and &quot;Socialism takes power away from the ruling class and distributes it evenly among the working class&quot; when the reality is that socialist governments stole the property of poor farmers (shooting or imprisoning those who objected) and gave it to favored political operatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T20:38:29-07:00","id":1511176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1510890-oh-glad-to-see-this-finally-come-out?p=1511043#post1511043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say daredevils get Dramatic Editing cheap, but rather that everyone else pays a surcharge, since daredevils pay the exact same default costs as standard talents or Aether era squires.<br /> <br /> Having gone over the final download, I have to say I'm disappointed with one thing and very angry with another.<br /> <br /> My disappointment is with the fact that, since the preview copy was released over the x-mas/new year's holiday, I got less than 1/3 of the way through the book before the errata period closed. I didn't even get to the Gifts, and it looks like no one else submitted Gift errata either, since all of the things I noticed are still in the book. In addition to Momentary Gifts that should be Constant and vice versa, it looks like in the 'low powered' era of Adventure!, mesmerists are able to create illusions the size of cities and break machines the size of a city with a simple Gift and a single dice roll.<br /> <br /> I'm quite angry with the fact that, despite raising the issue during both the Kickstarter manuscript and preview book errata phases, they didn't change one single word of the Socialism entry of the seven evil '-isms' section of the storyguiding chapter. They give us page after page on the evils of anti-Semitism, classism, fascism, heterosexism, racism, and sexism\u200b, but follow it up with half a page of pro-socialist hype. The Holocaust killed about 6.5 million people, while Communist governments have killed anywhere from 10 million to 110 million, depending on the source.<br /> <br /> We get pretty phrases like &quot;They sought the replacement of capitalism with something more equal and rational with shared wealth within a given society&quot; and &quot;Socialism takes power away from the ruling class and distributes it evenly among the working class&quot; when the reality is that socialist governments stole the property of poor farmers (shooting or imprisoning those who objected) and gave it to favored political operatives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey! Thanks so much for your feedback. We can't always implement everything that people submit as feedback, but we appreciate you taking the time to submit! We're sorry that you aren't happy with the product. You're free to use any part of the book that you like, and ignore the parts that you don't like. We even encourage folks to mix things up at their tables, pull rules from other games, and do whatever you like with the product now that you own it. I hope you're able to find some joy in the game despite its perceived flaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T21:21:34-07:00","id":1511180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1510890-oh-glad-to-see-this-finally-come-out?p=1511176#post1511176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey! Thanks so much for your feedback. We can't always implement everything that people submit as feedback, but we appreciate you taking the time to submit!</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully understand that not every piece of feedback can be implemented. My problem is that it was entirely possible to address the feedback. You wrote a half page entry on why Socialism was bad that didn't provide a single example of why Socialism was bad. As you yourselves stated at the beginning of the &quot;-isms&quot; section:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it can sometimes do a disservice to the people and cultures who suffered to simply gloss over the ugly parts of history because they make people uncomfortabl\u200be. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it does do a disservice to those who suffered, and yes, you repeatedly chose to gloss over an ugly part of history because it made you uncomfortabl\u200be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T12:18:05-07:00","id":1512900,"title":"","content":"Onyx Path products have a lot of politics in their games. I noticed that a minor feminist focused allegiance of well intentioned extremists from the first version of the game has seemingly been updated to be one of the player focus factions, like the Air Circus. I don't see the reason behind that, if it is so. A major conceit of the game is that the various player organizations are unusually egalitarian for their time. And the Aeon Society in particular would be on the forefront of the battle for gender equality. They also do cool stuff like fight people with zeppelin armadas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T13:24:56-07:00","id":1512905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1510890-oh-glad-to-see-this-finally-come-out?p=1512900#post1512900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Onyx Path products have a lot of politics in their games. I noticed that a minor feminist focused allegiance of well intentioned extremists from the first version of the game has seemingly been updated to be one of the player focus factions, like the Air Circus. I don't see the reason behind that, if it is so. A major conceit of the game is that the various player organizations are unusually egalitarian for their time. And the Aeon Society in particular would be on the forefront of the battle for gender equality. They also do cool stuff like fight people with zeppelin armadas.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole basis for feminism as practiced by Le Salon Des Femmes Nouvelles is fighting for gender equality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T18:51:52-07:00","id":1513145,"title":"","content":"Seems limited in scope, especially considering that one of the Aeon Society's hat is battling for progressive change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T06:22:35-07:00","id":1515108,"title":"","content":"Actually, it should be Le Salon Des Nouvelles Femmes. Nouvelles because the adjective is feminine and modifies Femmes, plus Nouvelle is one of those rare adjectives in French that comes before the noun it modifies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T18:10:55-07:00","id":1515195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1510890-oh-glad-to-see-this-finally-come-out?p=1515108#post1515108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it should be Le Salon Des Nouvelles Femmes. Nouvelles because the adjective is feminine and modifies Femmes, plus Nouvelle is one of those rare adjectives in French that comes before the noun it modifies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although you are correct regarding the typical position of nouvelle in French, you are incorrect in your statement since it ignores the historical context of la Femme Nouvelle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T15:30:36-07:00","id":1515488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkeydjie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1510890-oh-glad-to-see-this-finally-come-out?p=1515195#post1515195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although you are correct regarding the typical position of nouvelle in French, you are incorrect in your statement since it ignores the historical context of la Femme Nouvelle.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the historical context?<br /> <br /> Never mind. I just looked it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 06-18-2023, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T19:26:30-07:00","id":1515507,"title":"","content":"Also, nouvelle has two meanings, one being the opposite of old (vieille) and the other being the opposite of former or previous (ancienne). When it\u2019s used with the second meaning, you are absolutely right. Nouvelle does come after femmes, as in La Femme Nouvelle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 06-18-2023, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}